<info>
  <ul>
    <li><code>fez:animate="height"</code> - the element animates from its old to its new height whenever its content changes</li>
    <li>Built in, no wrapper component: put the attribute on any element in a template, or call <code>Fez.animateSize(node, 'height, duration=250')</code> on plain DOM</li>
    <li>Catches state re-renders, nested component renders and outside DOM changes (ResizeObserver, animates before paint, no flicker, no inline height left behind)</li>
    <li>Params: <code>duration</code>, <code>delay</code>, <code>easing</code>. <code>width</code> / <code>size</code> animate the other axis, <code>fez:animate="flip, height"</code> combines with list reorder</li>
  </ul>
</info>

<demo>
  <ui-auto-height></ui-auto-height>
</demo>

<script>
  init() {
    this.state.duration = 300
    this.state.easing = 'cubicOut'
    this.state.long = false
    this.state.paragraphs = [1]
    this.local.next = 2
  }

  add() {
    this.state.paragraphs.push(this.local.next++)
  }

  remove() {
    if (this.state.paragraphs.length > 1) this.state.paragraphs.pop()
  }

  toggleLong() {
    this.state.long = !this.state.long
  }
</script>

<style>
  .row { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .row label { color: #666; font-size: 14px; }
  .box {
    display: flow-root;
    padding: 4px 16px;
    background: #fff;
    border: 2px solid #ccd;
    border-radius: 6px;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
  }
  .box p { margin: 12px 0; }
</style>

<div class="row">
  <label>duration</label>
  <div>
    <select fez:bind="state.duration">
      <option value="100">100 ms</option>
      <option value="200">200 ms</option>
      <option value="300">300 ms</option>
      <option value="500">500 ms</option>
      <option value="800">800 ms</option>
      <option value="1500">1500 ms</option>
    </select>
    <label>easing</label>
    <select fez:bind="state.easing">
      <option>linear</option>
      <option>ease-in-out</option>
      <option>cubicOut</option>
      <option>quintOut</option>
      <option>expoOut</option>
      <option>backOut</option>
      <option>backInOut</option>
      <option>circOut</option>
    </select>
  </div>
  <div style="margin: 12px 0;">
    <button onclick="fez.add()">add paragraph</button>
    <button onclick="fez.remove()">remove paragraph</button>
    <button onclick="fez.toggleLong()">toggle long text</button>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="box" fez:animate="height, duration={state.duration}, easing={state.easing}">
  {#if state.long}
    <p>This is a much longer text that will cause the container to expand significantly. Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit.</p>
    <p>Sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Ut enim ad minim veniam, quis nostrud exercitation ullamco laboris nisi ut aliquip ex ea commodo consequat. Duis aute irure dolor in reprehenderit in voluptate velit esse cillum dolore eu fugiat nulla pariatur.</p>
    <p>Eu tempor nisi nostrud ipsum minim quis adipisicing cillum. Cupidatat labore consectetur dolor consectetur ipsum ea voluptate ea. Et fugiat quis ullamco eu irure ullamco qui cillum enim eu velit ea qui nulla.</p>
  {:else}
    {#each state.paragraphs as id}
      <p key="{id}" fez:in="fade, duration=200">Paragraph {id}. It contains some sample text to demonstrate the height animation.</p>
      <p>This is a much longer text that will cause the container to expand significantly. Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit.</p>
      <p>Sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Ut enim ad minim veniam, quis nostrud exercitation ullamco laboris nisi ut aliquip ex ea commodo consequat. Duis aute irure dolor in reprehenderit in voluptate velit esse cillum dolore eu fugiat nulla pariatur.</p>
    {/each}
  {/if}
</div>
